  title "The Drift of Broken Things"
  summary "Rend Kzulrora, a scarred orca, drifts beneath the Berg while teaching his young pod member Kzul-kzaith the hunting patterns of their people, including techniques inherited from the fallen Coldbringer Gnash Krukwark. The narrative explores the tension between orcas and penguins living in the Berg's tunnels, where a law of silence (Foedus∴silenti) now governs the penguin civilization following years of orca raids. Rend carries the weight of past conflicts—marked by penguin beaks on a cord and mysterious artifacts he refuses to use—while sensing a deeper wrongness settling over the Berg as both civilizations withdraw inward, their mutual scars becoming structural to their coexistence."
